# spike — Avalonia + AvaloniaEdit

Default launch runs the resident scratchpad prototype. It saves Markdown notes to `spikes/A/data/notes.json`, logs focus/input/material/autosave timings to `spikes/A/logs/`, and registers `Ctrl+Alt+Space` while the app is open. Drag only from the blue `DRAG NOTES HERE` strip; that keeps editor text selection available. Horizontal wheel tilts move at 120 logical pixels per notch and settle after 130 ms. `Esc` hides; tray menu or `Exit` quits.

This project uses cached Avalonia 12.1.4 and AvaloniaEdit 12.0.0. In a restricted shell, build without restore and opt out of Avalonia telemetry for this process:

```powershell
$env:AVALONIA_TELEMETRY_OPTOUT = '1'
dotnet build .\spikes\A\InputProbe.csproj --no-restore -p:UseAppHost=false -p:OutDir=bin/verify/
```

Launch modes from the repository root:

```powershell
$env:AVALONIA_TELEMETRY_OPTOUT = '1'
dotnet .\spikes\A\bin\verify\InputProbe.dll                 # app
dotnet .\spikes\A\bin\verify\InputProbe.dll --ui-smoke       # opens, logs template/focus/edit+undo/material/bounds, exits
dotnet .\spikes\A\bin\verify\InputProbe.dll --probe          # retained Avalonia/native event diagnostic
dotnet .\spikes\A\bin\verify\InputProbe.dll --smoke           # 17 fast model/editor/persistence checks
```

`--ui-smoke` uses a temporary JSON path and removes it on exit. It verifies the AvaloniaEdit template and programmatic document insert/undo; it does not substitute for physical typing, the tray/hotkey, material appearance, or mouse-driver validation. The regular log reports `TextArea.IsKeyboardFocusWithin` after deferred focus and logs each document change with that actual state.
