# Spike A report — T-002

Updated 2026-10-17. **Implemented and self-checked; WAITING ON USER for interactive acceptance.**

The revised mouse-only gate permits proceeding. The user log proves notched horizontal wheel delivery, not keyboard focus. The expanded prototype now builds offline and its runtime self-check records a focused, laid-out AvaloniaEdit editor. No final stack selection or full live acceptance is claimed.

## Gate 1 and focus

[Mouse evidence](GATE1-MOUSE.md): user log input-probe-20261017-013136.log contains 65 horizontal wheel events, native +120 (37) / -120 (28), corresponding Avalonia X=-1/+1 with pointer Mouse; no fractional values. All 824 original records had focused=False. Mouse model/driver unknown; user confirms a notched horizontal wheel. Touchpad is optional and untested under updated spec 4a.

The original App.axaml omitted AvaloniaEdit's theme include. Added the packaged Fluent editor theme and deferred TextArea.Focus(); diagnostic mode now also targets TextArea and logs text changes. In the final runtime check, editor focus-within=True, template visible=True, measured text view=True (700x524), programmatic insert=True and undo restoration=True. This establishes a working editor template/focus path; actual keyboard input still needs the user check.

## Outcomes by spec item

PASS below names the specific observed scope; IMPLEMENTED means live acceptance is pending.

| Item | Result / evidence |
|---|---|
| Pinned restore/build | PASS offline build, 0 warnings/errors; cached Avalonia 12.1.4, AvaloniaEdit 12.0.0. No new packages, no restore this turn. |
| Horizontal wheel delivery | PASS user-operated probe for ±1 notches only. Hi-res/inertial driver input untested. |
| Mouse carousel | IMPLEMENTED: 120 px/unit eased step, 130 ms idle-gap release; distance plus damped last-delta velocity select snap; mouse grab strip captures real press/release, 1:1 pointer delta, stale velocity cleared after pause. Actual direction/feel/capture pending user. |
| Momentum, snap/spring-back | IMPLEMENTED: brief bounded decaying momentum then eased snap; cancellation springs to current note. This is disposable tuning, not a physics library or benchmarked fluidity. |
| Rubber band / create / prune | IMPLEMENTED: exponential edge resistance bounded near 180 px; raw newest overscroll past 170 px creates one note. Blank interior notes prune at safe creation boundary; trailing blank retained. Model predicates/pruning pass; physical trigger untested. |
| Wrapping / vertical scroll / selection | Wrapping visible in render preview. Dedicated grab strip separates drag from editor selection; vertical wheel is not consumed by carousel. Live scroll/selection check pending. |
| Resident frameless + tray + hotkey | Frame-free window, generated tray icon/menu, RegisterHotKey and retained Hide/Show implemented. Primary chord collides (1409); Ctrl+Alt+Shift+A fallback registration PASS. Same window hide/show and focus restoration PASS by method invocation, with one-time initialization guard. Physical hotkey delivery/tray access pending. |
| Transparent / Acrylic / Mica | Runtime ActualTransparencyLevel matched all 3 requested values. Text clarity and Windows compositor appearance unverified. Cards intentionally retain a translucent dark fill for readable text. |
| Decorated Markdown, visible markers | Framework render shows different heading levels, bold/italic/strike and visible markers. Small line regex transformer, not full Markdown parsing. |
| Clickable checkbox, undo/caret | Source replacement, caret preservation and undo model checks PASS. Click hit-test uses document coordinates including scroll offset; wrapped/scrolled physical clicking pending. |
| Tab/Shift+Tab selection indent | Multi-line indent, grouped undo and outdent checks PASS; physical key routing/selection pending. |
| Python fenced syntax | Framework render shows keyword/string coloring inside python fence, rest Markdown. Bounded local range-aware regex highlighter, no new grammar package. Nested/complex Python syntax not promised. |
| Autosave/restore | JSON content/order roundtrip PASS; temporary-file replacement. Actual quit/relaunch user check pending. Current note index/undo history not persisted. Synchronous save per edit is a prototype limitation. |
| Folding / line numbers | Line numbers visible; fence fold manager/control compiled. Interactive folding pending; ranges refreshed on install, not live edits. |
| Smoke checks | 15/15 model/editor/store checks PASS in 54.0 ms. UI self-check exit 0. Twelve separate interactive checks authored, not run by Director. |
| Screenshot evidence | [Framework-rendered preview](render-preview.png) inspected. It is not a desktop/compositor screenshot and does not validate backdrops. |

## Measurements

Debug framework-dependent process on Windows 10.0.26340, .NET SDK 10.0.402 / runtime 10.0.13, 96 DPI. Single process samples, not a statistical benchmark or cold-cache test.

| Measurement | Observed result / limit |
|---|---|
| Main entry to Opened | 976.0 ms final run (excludes dotnet host startup) |
| Main entry to reported focus | 1165.0 ms final run; physical typing and first paint not timed |
| Settled sample memory | Private bytes 116,535,296 (~111.1 MiB); working set 160,378,880 (~153.0 MiB), about 3.1 s after Main; not long-idle RAM |
| Hide method dispatch | 4.22 ms; excludes proof of desktop disappearance |
| Show method dispatch | 2.270 ms; focus reported shortly afterward; not hotkey-to-visible latency |
| Hotkey-to-visible/focused | UNMEASURED physical input latency |
| Build loop | Earlier warm rebuild ~2.57 s; final build 22.44 s, zero warnings/errors; environmental variability observed |

Evidence: [build](build-mouse.txt), [15 smoke results](smoke-mouse.txt), [runtime UI log](ui-smoke-log.txt). Earlier build-block/build-success artifacts retain the history and are superseded by build-mouse.txt.

## Review and remaining work

One Luna high worker owned spikes/A for implementation; Director integrated/reviewed after handoff. Review corrected clipped-strip transforms/easing, animation interruption, stale drag velocity, note-pruning indexes, save ordering, hotkey lifecycle/duplicate Opened, fallback chord, runtime paths, focus/style setup and scroll-aware checkbox coordinates. No system software or packages added. No B edits or shared STATUS writes.

No final go/no-go before user acceptance. Would I build the real app on this? **Avalonia remains plausible, but I would first validate the mouse interaction and desktop shell using this prototype.** Editor extension work is manageable here; the measured Debug startup and synchronous persistence still need production-oriented work before speed claims.

Rough planning estimate after user feedback: half a day to a day for interaction tuning and fixes; several days for a production-shaped persistence/input/editor pass before deeper performance comparison. This is an uncertain estimate, not measured development effort or a promise of a finished app.

## Current next step

Run the DLL command and the 12 checks in [MANUAL-CHECKS.md](MANUAL-CHECKS.md); exact current launch/chord/log instructions are at the end of "'`.coord/status-A.md`. Return PASS/FAIL observations and the newest spikes/A/logs/spike-*.log, plus mouse model/driver/scaling. Director stopped when interactive validation became necessary, per user instruction. Local commit remains blocked by .git write denial; manager retry commands are recorded in status-A.md.
